1
00:00:12,367 --> 00:00:13,567
(The second commercial district)

2
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:15,237
(Street Beer Festival)

3
00:00:16,507 --> 00:00:18,907
(Two teams compete with the same price.)

4
00:00:19,177 --> 00:00:22,647
(One team closes its business.)

5
00:00:22,807 --> 00:00:25,647
(First half, Kim Kwan Hoon versus Lee Yeon Bok)

6
00:00:25,647 --> 00:00:27,947
(BokBok wins.)

7
00:00:28,287 --> 00:00:30,517
(Orders start flowing in as soon as the second half starts.)

8
00:00:30,517 --> 00:00:33,657
(BokBok is sold out due to running out of ingredients.)

9
00:00:33,927 --> 00:00:37,027
(Everything About Tteokbokki begins a fierce comeback.)

10
00:00:37,027 --> 00:00:40,627
We have nothing left to sell while they'll keep getting orders.

11
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:44,297
Everything About Tteokbokki...

12
00:00:44,297 --> 00:00:48,367
(Taking the lead by 60 dollars)

13
00:00:50,107 --> 00:00:52,477
- What will be the result?
- I can't wait to find out.

14
00:00:52,477 --> 00:00:53,477
(Lee Yeon Bok versus Kim Kwan Hoon)

15
00:00:53,477 --> 00:00:54,977
- Everything About Tteokbokki.
- Well done.

16
00:00:55,807 --> 00:00:56,847
BokBok.

17
00:00:58,277 --> 00:01:01,247
(The match between the ultimate champions)

18
00:01:02,547 --> 00:01:05,687
In the 2nd half of the 20-dollar price range...

19
00:01:05,687 --> 00:01:07,827
(The second half result to determine the winner)

20
00:01:08,027 --> 00:01:09,027
BokBok.

21
00:01:09,827 --> 00:01:11,427
Everything About Tteokbokki.

22
00:01:13,197 --> 00:01:15,527
Their sales are the same.

23
00:01:15,527 --> 00:01:16,827
(Their sales are the same.)

24
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:24,407
How is that possible?

25
00:01:26,115 --> 00:01:27,277
Their sales are the same?

26
00:01:29,207 --> 00:01:31,417
I thought that we lost the second half.

27
00:01:31,817 --> 00:01:33,317
I couldn't understand.

28
00:01:34,487 --> 00:01:36,817
(Right before the end of the second half)

29
00:01:36,817 --> 00:01:40,227
(Everything About Tteokbokki was taking the lead by 60 dollars.)

30
00:01:41,187 --> 00:01:43,827
While we were winning, when I glanced at Lee Yeon Bok,

31
00:01:43,827 --> 00:01:44,857
he was cleaning up.

32
00:01:45,157 --> 00:01:47,227
So I thought, "All right, we won."

33
00:01:48,167 --> 00:01:50,167
We didn't get our order yet.

34
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:52,897
- Is it possible to cancel it?
- Yes, you can cancel it. I'm sorry.

35
00:01:53,497 --> 00:01:57,137
(A refund customer appears.)

36
00:01:57,707 --> 00:02:00,907
(The second refund customer appears.)

37
00:02:01,647 --> 00:02:05,647
(Refunds start coming in one after the other.)

38
00:02:06,177 --> 00:02:08,847
(Someone didn't take their order.)

39
00:02:10,117 --> 00:02:14,687
(And there was a third refund.)

40
00:02:15,827 --> 00:02:18,297
(Currently, their sales are the same.)

41
00:02:18,827 --> 00:02:19,897
It was a bummer.

42
00:02:20,897 --> 00:02:22,297
Their sales are the same. They're tied.

43
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:23,997
It'll be decided by customer ratings.

44
00:02:24,537 --> 00:02:26,167
This is so nerve-racking.

45
00:02:27,267 --> 00:02:29,267
I'll announce the customer ratings.

46
00:02:30,877 --> 00:02:31,937
BokBok.

47
00:02:31,937 --> 00:02:38,417
(BokBok, 2nd half sales: 840 dollars)

48
00:02:38,417 --> 00:02:39,447
BokBok.

49
00:02:42,247 --> 00:02:43,247
Four points.

50
00:02:43,247 --> 00:02:47,187
(Customer ratings: 4 points)

51
00:02:47,287 --> 00:02:48,687
Everything About Tteokbokki.

52
00:02:48,687 --> 00:02:55,727
(Everything About Tteokbokki, 2nd half sales: 840 dollars)

53
00:02:55,767 --> 00:02:57,167
It's 3.7 points.

54
00:02:57,167 --> 00:02:58,597
(Customer ratings: 3.7 points)

55
00:02:58,597 --> 00:03:00,137
- With a difference of 0.3 points, - That was close.

56
00:03:00,137 --> 00:03:01,467
BokBok wins.

57
00:03:01,467 --> 00:03:02,767
(BokBok is the final winner with 2 to 0.)

58
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:05,507
The final winner in the 20-dollar price range is BokBok.

59
00:03:06,737 --> 00:03:10,047
- Well done.
- Well done.

60
00:03:10,317 --> 00:03:11,447
I hope that you win.

61
00:03:11,577 --> 00:03:13,317
- I'm sorry.
- Please win for us.

62
00:03:17,057 --> 00:03:18,117
Well done, everyone.

63
00:03:19,687 --> 00:03:21,627
This experience taught me...

64
00:03:22,227 --> 00:03:24,897
a huge lesson all over again.

65
00:03:25,697 --> 00:03:28,467
It really reminded me just how important ratings are.

66
00:03:28,827 --> 00:03:31,997
Next time, we'll have to come up with a better strategy.

67
00:03:34,237 --> 00:03:36,337
We would've won if the two bowls hadn't been canceled.

68
00:03:39,107 --> 00:03:40,547
- We gave it everything we had.
- We did our best.

69
00:03:40,547 --> 00:03:42,177
(Everything About Tteokbokki, BokBok)

70
00:03:42,447 --> 00:03:43,747
More than anything,

71
00:03:43,747 --> 00:03:46,417
even though we lost, we fought a good battle.

72
00:03:46,717 --> 00:03:49,247
I don't have any regrets.

73
00:03:49,587 --> 00:03:53,087
We did an amazing job, especially under those circumstances.

74
00:03:53,457 --> 00:03:57,257
It was a tough challenge, but we worked together well...

75
00:03:57,657 --> 00:04:00,257
and gave it our best.

76
00:04:00,897 --> 00:04:02,197
That's what I kept thinking.

77
00:04:04,737 --> 00:04:07,807
(Today's matchup continues.)

78
00:04:07,807 --> 00:04:09,437
(1-on-1 same price battle)

79
00:04:09,437 --> 00:04:13,207
The matchup I was most curious about was...

80
00:04:14,907 --> 00:04:18,147
Gotgan that makes Korean food...

81
00:04:20,787 --> 00:04:22,417
Gotgan and The Star In My Heart.

82
00:04:23,787 --> 00:04:26,287
When Chef Jo Seo Hyung picked Gotgan,

83
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:28,157
I thought that it'd be really fun.

84
00:04:29,127 --> 00:04:31,027
(1-on-1 same price battle, The Star In My Heart)

85
00:04:31,027 --> 00:04:33,767
(The Star In My Heart picked Gotgan.)

86
00:04:33,927 --> 00:04:34,967
I knew it.

87
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:37,737
- They're true rivals.
- This will be fun.

88
00:04:37,967 --> 00:04:39,097
It's a derby.

89
00:04:39,137 --> 00:04:40,167
A Korean cuisine derby.

90
00:04:40,937 --> 00:04:41,967
A true Korean food showdown.

91
00:04:42,807 --> 00:04:46,377
I want to have a fun dance with Korean food.

92
00:04:46,477 --> 00:04:47,977
(Laughing)

93
00:04:47,977 --> 00:04:49,507
I'm very happy...

94
00:04:49,947 --> 00:04:51,747
that she chose us. I like how bold she is.

95
00:04:51,747 --> 00:04:53,577
Let's go for a head-to-head fight.

96
00:04:54,847 --> 00:04:56,617
I've been cooking Korean food for a long time,

97
00:04:56,887 --> 00:04:59,417
but the elder ladies' seasoning,

98
00:04:59,687 --> 00:05:01,187
balance, and homemade touch...

99
00:05:01,757 --> 00:05:03,257
That territory is intimidating.

100
00:05:04,797 --> 00:05:08,127
(Gotgan, led by the original Imokase)

101
00:05:08,797 --> 00:05:10,097
So I was intimidated.

102
00:05:11,267 --> 00:05:13,367
If it's a mountain I have to climb someday,

103
00:05:13,497 --> 00:05:14,907
I might as well climb it sooner than later.

104
00:05:15,807 --> 00:05:18,377
Chef Jo Seo Hyung has been in this business for a long time,

105
00:05:18,577 --> 00:05:19,807
but I've been doing it longer.

106
00:05:20,707 --> 00:05:22,907
I'll do my best to rise to the challenge.

107
00:05:23,777 --> 00:05:27,047
In the ten-dollar range, The Star In My Heart versus Gotgan.

108
00:05:27,077 --> 00:05:29,387
- The Star In My Heart.
- This is a big match.

109
00:05:29,387 --> 00:05:30,857
(Who will be the winner of the Korean food showdown?)

110
00:05:32,387 --> 00:05:33,957
Let's put this out first.

111
00:05:39,057 --> 00:05:40,897
- My gosh.
- Oh, my.

112
00:05:41,097 --> 00:05:43,867
- They're taking out the equipment.
- They prepared a lot.

113
00:05:43,937 --> 00:05:45,737
We almost made that too, but we couldn't be bothered.

114
00:05:46,997 --> 00:05:48,907
(It's a nice day to cook.)

115
00:05:48,907 --> 00:05:50,507
Don't block the storefront.

116
00:05:52,207 --> 00:05:53,707
- Should I put it here?
- Yes.

117
00:05:54,447 --> 00:05:56,777
What do you call it? We made a flyer.

118
00:05:56,777 --> 00:05:58,517
- No, we made banners.
- We made banners.

119
00:05:58,517 --> 00:05:59,547
(Gotgan prepared eye-catching banners.)

120
00:05:59,577 --> 00:06:01,647
Putting my photo on it...

121
00:06:01,647 --> 00:06:04,157
with big texts helped it stand out.

122
00:06:04,157 --> 00:06:05,587
(It's a nice day to cook.)

123
00:06:05,587 --> 00:06:07,987
(A menu that makes you crave beer?)

124
00:06:08,427 --> 00:06:09,827
Just because I cook Korean food doesn't mean...

125
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:11,627
that I only serve set meals.

126
00:06:12,127 --> 00:06:13,627
This is a beer festival.

127
00:06:14,027 --> 00:06:18,597
So I wanted to serve food that goes well with beer.

128
00:06:19,967 --> 00:06:23,537
For the first half, we're serving fried suyuk and fried pork skin.

129
00:06:28,177 --> 00:06:30,647
She has a big container. Should I ask if I can borrow it?

130
00:06:31,377 --> 00:06:32,847
- Should I ask her for it?
- From where?

131
00:06:32,917 --> 00:06:35,047
- The stall next door.
- No way.

132
00:06:36,047 --> 00:06:37,087
Why not?

133
00:06:40,587 --> 00:06:41,657
Chef Jo.

134
00:06:41,857 --> 00:06:43,897
Are you not using that white kimchi container?

135
00:06:43,897 --> 00:06:45,557
Mom, we don't need any kimchi container.

136
00:06:45,557 --> 00:06:48,067
I want to keep the batter in it.

137
00:06:48,167 --> 00:06:49,597
Don't borrow it from her.

138
00:06:50,837 --> 00:06:52,237
We'll figure out our own way.

139
00:06:52,237 --> 00:06:54,567
Why would you borrow from the team we're competing with?

140
00:06:55,237 --> 00:06:56,807
I'm the type of person...

141
00:06:57,507 --> 00:07:00,707
who can't sleep...

142
00:07:00,707 --> 00:07:03,917
if I lose a competition like this.

143
00:07:05,447 --> 00:07:07,617
What's wrong with borrowing it? She's not using it.

144
00:07:08,987 --> 00:07:10,817
We have to beat the stall next door.

145
00:07:10,817 --> 00:07:11,987
- I know.
- If we lose,

146
00:07:11,987 --> 00:07:13,117
I won't be able to sleep.

147
00:07:13,117 --> 00:07:15,227
(Gotgan is determined to win today.)

148
00:07:16,627 --> 00:07:18,027
When I did the math,

149
00:07:18,957 --> 00:07:21,567
I realized we'd have to fry well over...

150
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:23,427
a thousand bite-sized pieces of pork skin.

151
00:07:23,667 --> 00:07:26,197
Mom, the oil is ready. We have to deep-fry all of these.

152
00:07:26,197 --> 00:07:27,367
(Five ingredients to deep-fry)

153
00:07:27,667 --> 00:07:30,467
(All ingredients are partially fried in advance.)

154
00:07:33,107 --> 00:07:36,247
(Fried suyuk)

155
00:07:36,947 --> 00:07:39,017
Ginseng won't take long. I'm so relieved.

156
00:07:39,447 --> 00:07:41,487
It's done. It's going well.

157
00:07:42,047 --> 00:07:43,517
Gosh, it looks nice.

158
00:07:43,957 --> 00:07:45,487
Mom, we can keep doing it that way.

159
00:07:46,287 --> 00:07:47,287
Is this enough?

160
00:07:50,287 --> 00:07:52,297
Gosh, you prepared a lot.

161
00:07:53,997 --> 00:07:54,997
Here you go.

162
00:08:01,951 --> 00:08:03,291
Is everything boiling nicely?

163
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:05,961
The frying is going well so far.

164
00:08:07,091 --> 00:08:08,361
I can smell your delicious food all the way over here.

165
00:08:09,091 --> 00:08:12,361
- I want a piece of your fried food.
- We want some fried food.

166
00:08:13,301 --> 00:08:15,371
I guess everyone is thinking the same thing.

167
00:08:15,371 --> 00:08:17,401
- Since it's a festival...
- Fried food.

168
00:08:17,971 --> 00:08:20,741
(Fried food)

169
00:08:21,111 --> 00:08:24,641
(10 out of 18 teams are preparing fried food.)

170
00:08:25,111 --> 00:08:26,611
It looks like everyone is frying something today.

171
00:08:30,281 --> 00:08:31,451
- Jae Beom.
- Yes?

172
00:08:31,521 --> 00:08:32,781
Please stir-fry the meat first.

173
00:08:32,951 --> 00:08:33,991
Okay.

174
00:08:35,921 --> 00:08:38,191
Great. It's a chance to add more smoky flavor.

175
00:08:44,561 --> 00:08:45,761
For the first half, we're serving...

176
00:08:45,761 --> 00:08:47,971
a mountain of spicy stir-fried pork and gimbap.

177
00:08:48,301 --> 00:08:50,971
When I thought about what everyone else would make,

178
00:08:51,401 --> 00:08:54,971
I didn't think many would go with rice dishes.

179
00:08:55,271 --> 00:08:57,071
Most customers coming around 5pm will...

180
00:08:57,341 --> 00:08:58,541
probably want something...

181
00:08:58,541 --> 00:09:00,711
that works as a meal and a snack to go with beer.

182
00:09:01,811 --> 00:09:03,781
That's where I knew we had a chance.

183
00:09:04,181 --> 00:09:07,891
(Targeting a niche market with a rice-based dish)

184
00:09:08,221 --> 00:09:10,121
I was wondering why it was so spicy.

185
00:09:10,291 --> 00:09:12,191
I realized there was Cheongyang chili on one side.

186
00:09:14,531 --> 00:09:16,291
- Smoky flavor is what I wanted.
- Smoky flavor.

187
00:09:17,191 --> 00:09:20,401
(Preparing a spicy dish to cut through the heavy fried food)

188
00:09:20,401 --> 00:09:22,501
It smells so delicious.

189
00:09:23,601 --> 00:09:25,371
(Seasonal perilla sprouts, sesame seeds,)

190
00:09:25,371 --> 00:09:27,101
(spicy stir-fried pork, gimbap)

191
00:09:27,341 --> 00:09:30,511
(A mountain of spicy stir-fried pork and sesame gimbap for 10 dollars)

192
00:09:30,741 --> 00:09:31,741
Chef?

193
00:09:32,641 --> 00:09:34,851
We have 77 rolls so far.

194
00:09:35,851 --> 00:09:37,011
Seventy-seven rolls.

195
00:09:38,051 --> 00:09:40,281
We have 77 rolls so far.

196
00:09:40,421 --> 00:09:41,591
Seventy-seven rolls.

197
00:09:42,191 --> 00:09:43,591
That's exactly what we expected.

198
00:09:45,091 --> 00:09:46,091
Seventy-seven rolls.

199
00:09:46,091 --> 00:09:47,091
(Exchanging looks)

200
00:09:48,191 --> 00:09:49,191
Come here for a second.

201
00:09:50,461 --> 00:09:52,561
- What?
- Seventy-seven rolls?

202
00:09:52,561 --> 00:09:54,531
- That means 77 servings.
- Yes.

203
00:09:54,871 --> 00:09:56,471
We can make up to 120 servings.

204
00:09:57,501 --> 00:09:58,571
In that case...

205
00:09:59,941 --> 00:10:03,871
We could beat them with quantity as long as we sell them.

206
00:10:03,871 --> 00:10:05,111
That's what I kept thinking.

207
00:10:08,881 --> 00:10:12,781
(They can also see the other side.)

208
00:10:17,361 --> 00:10:18,691
This might overflow.

209
00:10:22,131 --> 00:10:23,731
You're preparing so much meat.

210
00:10:24,201 --> 00:10:26,061
How many servings is that?

211
00:10:27,371 --> 00:10:28,771
(Pretending not to notice)

212
00:10:28,771 --> 00:10:30,501
How many servings is that?

213
00:10:32,001 --> 00:10:34,171
That's enough for 200 people.

214
00:10:38,241 --> 00:10:40,681
(Remaining silent)

215
00:10:40,951 --> 00:10:43,081
What if they're preparing 150 servings?

216
00:10:43,951 --> 00:10:46,621
Why are they making so much food?

217
00:10:47,821 --> 00:10:50,591
(Street Arena)

218
00:10:50,591 --> 00:10:54,591
Round 2 of 1-on-1 same price battle,

219
00:10:54,731 --> 00:10:56,791
the first half will start now.

220
00:10:56,791 --> 00:10:58,961
(1-on-1 same price battle business starts.)

221
00:10:59,831 --> 00:11:01,401
Good luck, Chef Kim.

222
00:11:01,601 --> 00:11:02,601
Good luck to you.

223
00:11:03,701 --> 00:11:04,741
Good luck.

224
00:11:05,641 --> 00:11:06,741
Let's do our best.

225
00:11:07,711 --> 00:11:09,171
Let's start from there.

226
00:11:09,971 --> 00:11:12,281
The 1st half and the 2nd half menu are...

227
00:11:12,281 --> 00:11:14,481
- different.
- I see.

228
00:11:14,651 --> 00:11:17,581
This is amazing. It looks very fun.

229
00:11:17,781 --> 00:11:19,451
Everything looks delicious.

230
00:11:20,181 --> 00:11:21,291
What should we order?

231
00:11:22,251 --> 00:11:24,561
(Korean food showdown, Kim Mi Ryeong versus Jo Seo Hyung)

232
00:11:24,721 --> 00:11:26,591
(Fried suyuk and pork skin versus a mountain...)

233
00:11:26,591 --> 00:11:28,491
(of spicy stir-fried pork and sesame gimbap)

234
00:11:29,491 --> 00:11:32,531
(Lee Jun Seong at Gotgan is waiting for customers.)

235
00:11:35,331 --> 00:11:37,771
Gosh, it's so empty.

236
00:11:39,471 --> 00:11:41,571
The stall next to us had a lot of decoration.

237
00:11:43,511 --> 00:11:46,441
It feels so empty because we don't have much set up.

238
00:11:47,481 --> 00:11:49,151
Wait, it's way too empty.

239
00:11:49,351 --> 00:11:50,351
Mom.

240
00:11:50,611 --> 00:11:51,981
- This won't work.
- What?

241
00:11:51,981 --> 00:11:52,981
It's too empty.

242
00:11:53,251 --> 00:11:54,891
Fill the empty spot with cutlassfish.

243
00:11:57,991 --> 00:12:00,561
We put out the boneless cutlassfish we had prepared for dinner.

244
00:12:00,561 --> 00:12:03,461
It fills up the space and...

245
00:12:03,491 --> 00:12:05,531
- And it works as promotion.
- We're making this for dinner.

246
00:12:05,531 --> 00:12:08,401
Instead of going somewhere else, come and have this for dinner.

247
00:12:08,501 --> 00:12:11,171
It could give them a reason to come back.

248
00:12:12,441 --> 00:12:14,441
Gosh, it's Imokase.

249
00:12:14,441 --> 00:12:16,111
- My gosh.
- The 1st 60 people?

250
00:12:16,671 --> 00:12:18,281
The 1st 60 people?

251
00:12:18,281 --> 00:12:21,781
We're offering complimentary fried ginseng to the 1st 60 customers.

252
00:12:21,781 --> 00:12:25,381
(Fried ginseng prepared by Imokase to the 1st 60 people)

253
00:12:25,381 --> 00:12:28,621
We're offering complimentary fried ginseng to the 1st 60 customers.

254
00:12:29,621 --> 00:12:30,991
By the way, the booth next door...

255
00:12:30,991 --> 00:12:32,861
is giving out fried ginseng.

256
00:12:32,861 --> 00:12:35,291
- Fried ginseng?
- On a 1st-come, 1st-served basis.

257
00:12:36,961 --> 00:12:38,601
I don't think they can manage it at that price.

