777
00:34:11,291 --> 00:34:12,591
Only 30 minutes before the 2nd half starts?

778
00:34:12,591 --> 00:34:13,661
I can't do this.

779
00:34:14,061 --> 00:34:15,191
I'm worried.

780
00:34:15,391 --> 00:34:17,731
It all comes down to who sends out the dishes faster.

781
00:34:19,001 --> 00:34:20,401
I'll keep them coming as fast as I can.

782
00:34:35,311 --> 00:34:37,011
(Sighing)

783
00:34:39,321 --> 00:34:42,151
(The 2nd half of the 18-dollar price range)

784
00:34:42,921 --> 00:34:47,021
(Number One's mala skewers versus Koony's American Street Food Box)

785
00:34:47,291 --> 00:34:50,431
Number One's mala skewers look good,

786
00:34:50,431 --> 00:34:51,431
but the queue is too long.

787
00:34:51,561 --> 00:34:53,431
Do you mean the order queue?

788
00:34:53,431 --> 00:34:55,061
The queue to order is already long.

789
00:34:55,701 --> 00:34:59,601
(Both teams have a long queue.)

790
00:35:00,041 --> 00:35:01,271
- What?
- Please confirm your order.

791
00:35:01,271 --> 00:35:02,511
It's 18 dollars for 20.

792
00:35:02,971 --> 00:35:04,171
It's very cost-effective.

793
00:35:06,741 --> 00:35:08,181
Is the portion big?

794
00:35:08,541 --> 00:35:10,081
- Please confirm your order.
- It's those.

795
00:35:10,351 --> 00:35:11,751
I see.

796
00:35:12,481 --> 00:35:14,621
They opened one at Bupyeong Station, and it's so good.

797
00:35:14,721 --> 00:35:15,751
Take it.

798
00:35:16,691 --> 00:35:17,991
For the second half,

799
00:35:18,651 --> 00:35:20,461
we're selling mala skewers.

800
00:35:21,221 --> 00:35:26,661
(Mala skewers)

801
00:35:27,101 --> 00:35:28,401
Mala skewers are one...

802
00:35:28,401 --> 00:35:30,931
of the most trending foods nowadays.

803
00:35:32,341 --> 00:35:33,501
It's mala skewers.

804
00:35:33,801 --> 00:35:34,971
- What?
- Mala skewers.

805
00:35:34,971 --> 00:35:36,111
- Where?
- Over there.

806
00:35:36,111 --> 00:35:38,071
- I told you it was mala skewers.
- It's mala.

807
00:35:38,071 --> 00:35:40,511
I told you just now. They sell 8 for 20 dollars or something.

808
00:35:40,511 --> 00:35:41,981
- Or 15 dollars.
- I need to try it.

809
00:35:42,781 --> 00:35:45,581
(The desire hunter competes with the popular food.)

810
00:35:48,121 --> 00:35:49,791
Eighteen-dollar price range.

811
00:35:50,291 --> 00:35:53,961
Number One is leading Koony by one plate.

812
00:35:53,961 --> 00:35:56,131
(Current sales count: Number One, 18, Koony, 17)

813
00:35:56,591 --> 00:35:58,431
- What's the difference?
- One plate.

814
00:35:59,861 --> 00:36:01,901
I kept sighing.

815
00:36:03,831 --> 00:36:05,641
Tae Hee, tell them about fishcake every now and then.

816
00:36:06,941 --> 00:36:08,001
Tae Hee, tell them about fishcake...

817
00:36:08,001 --> 00:36:09,071
- every now and then.
- Okay.

818
00:36:09,411 --> 00:36:12,641
We prepared an assortment of different street foods.

819
00:36:12,641 --> 00:36:14,641
(Garlic shrimp noodles, potato wedges, guacamole, hot dog)

820
00:36:14,641 --> 00:36:15,711
(Pulled pork: Southern American style barbecue...)

821
00:36:15,711 --> 00:36:16,751
(which is shredded along the grain.)

822
00:36:17,651 --> 00:36:19,221
(And...)

823
00:36:19,951 --> 00:36:23,191
(Fishcake)

824
00:36:23,321 --> 00:36:25,721
I thought it'd be cold during the second half.

825
00:36:26,791 --> 00:36:29,261
So I prepared fishcakes as the hidden free menu.

826
00:36:30,831 --> 00:36:34,001
(The fishcake broth has been boiling since the first half.)

827
00:36:34,361 --> 00:36:36,331
Tae Hee, let's carry the broth together.

828
00:36:38,001 --> 00:36:39,071
Watch out.

829
00:36:39,071 --> 00:36:40,641
(They placed the fishcakes, their secret weapon, in front.)

830
00:36:41,501 --> 00:36:43,341
When the steam rises...

831
00:36:43,441 --> 00:36:45,641
in the lighting in the evening,

832
00:36:45,641 --> 00:36:48,211
the sight alone catches your eyes.

833
00:36:48,411 --> 00:36:50,011
You don't expect...

834
00:36:50,011 --> 00:36:52,951
American Street Food Box and fishcakes to go well together.

835
00:36:54,281 --> 00:36:57,491
But I think this is what makes festivals fun.

836
00:36:59,191 --> 00:37:01,461
I guess the hidden free menu is the fishcakes.

837
00:37:01,591 --> 00:37:03,091
- Did you take your fishcake?
- No.

838
00:37:03,091 --> 00:37:04,391
It's on the house.

839
00:37:04,391 --> 00:37:05,901
- Really? Thank you.
- Yes.

840
00:37:05,901 --> 00:37:07,831
Some even bought the menu...

841
00:37:07,831 --> 00:37:09,201
to eat the fishcake.

842
00:37:09,771 --> 00:37:11,271
Do you sell just the fishcakes?

843
00:37:11,271 --> 00:37:12,601
We don't.

844
00:37:12,601 --> 00:37:15,341
It's complimentary for those who order from us.

845
00:37:15,811 --> 00:37:18,141
You can take one each after buying our food.

846
00:37:19,081 --> 00:37:21,741
It's a good idea to give out something with soup.

847
00:37:25,011 --> 00:37:26,551
I'm glad they gave out fishcakes.

848
00:37:27,121 --> 00:37:28,381
- Sorry?
- I'm glad they gave out fishcakes.

849
00:37:28,381 --> 00:37:30,191
You need warm soup like this.

850
00:37:31,091 --> 00:37:32,861
How are you?

851
00:37:34,161 --> 00:37:37,261
(Number One)

852
00:37:37,291 --> 00:37:39,461
The stall next to us gives out fishcakes.

853
00:37:40,601 --> 00:37:43,771
Where do I get unlimited popcorn? Will you give it here?

854
00:37:43,771 --> 00:37:45,431
- Popcorn...
- Once you finish it,

855
00:37:45,431 --> 00:37:47,101
bring back the empty plate, and I'll refill it.

856
00:37:48,101 --> 00:37:50,111
You don't give out nachos anymore, do you?

857
00:37:50,111 --> 00:37:51,771
I'll give you some popcorn instead.

858
00:37:51,771 --> 00:37:52,841
Thank you.

859
00:37:53,081 --> 00:37:55,041
We're using the same strategy as the first half.

860
00:37:55,711 --> 00:37:58,111
I prepared unlimited mala popcorn.

861
00:38:03,891 --> 00:38:06,521
(Mala popcorn against fishcakes)

862
00:38:06,761 --> 00:38:09,131
Mala popcorn? They give popcorn.

863
00:38:09,291 --> 00:38:10,831
It's 20 skewers.

864
00:38:11,231 --> 00:38:13,261
They give mala popcorn too.

865
00:38:14,761 --> 00:38:16,201
Popcorn too?

866
00:38:16,201 --> 00:38:17,631
I think they give us 30 of it.

867
00:38:19,301 --> 00:38:20,501
Enjoy.

868
00:38:20,501 --> 00:38:22,271
(Current sales count: 30 for both teams)

869
00:38:23,241 --> 00:38:25,111
(Pouring)

870
00:38:26,641 --> 00:38:28,641
- Thank you, enjoy.
- Thank you.

871
00:38:28,641 --> 00:38:30,451
- Sung Hoon, refill coleslaw.
- Okay.

872
00:38:30,451 --> 00:38:31,451
(The order sheets pour out nonstop.)

873
00:38:31,881 --> 00:38:33,021
It's sold out?

874
00:38:34,451 --> 00:38:36,051
Is it sold out if the kiosk says so?

875
00:38:36,351 --> 00:38:38,251
- Does it say sold out?
- Yes.

876
00:38:39,461 --> 00:38:41,061
The kiosk says we're sold out.

877
00:38:41,061 --> 00:38:42,161
- Yes, I cut it off.
- Is it right?

878
00:38:42,161 --> 00:38:43,231
We have too many orders.

879
00:38:43,731 --> 00:38:44,891
Is it not sold out?

880
00:38:44,891 --> 00:38:47,461
We have a lot of orders backed up,

881
00:38:47,801 --> 00:38:52,031
so we can accept only until here. I'm sorry.

882
00:38:52,671 --> 00:38:54,141
I couldn't handle it.

883
00:38:55,471 --> 00:38:57,671
They cut off their orders, right?

884
00:39:01,411 --> 00:39:03,251
- Did they stop?
- What?

885
00:39:04,151 --> 00:39:05,151
They're not doing anything.

886
00:39:05,781 --> 00:39:07,621
A mental breakdown...

887
00:39:07,621 --> 00:39:09,791
No. They couldn't be ready for the dishes.

888
00:39:10,951 --> 00:39:12,151
They're having trouble keeping up with making the dishes.

889
00:39:13,061 --> 00:39:16,091
I heard them saying, "We need to stop the orders."

890
00:39:16,391 --> 00:39:18,731
"We need to stop accepting orders."

891
00:39:18,831 --> 00:39:20,801
You can move quickly...

892
00:39:20,801 --> 00:39:22,501
when things run smoothly.

893
00:39:23,731 --> 00:39:24,871
But they were moving very slowly.

894
00:39:27,871 --> 00:39:28,901
Like this.

895
00:39:30,211 --> 00:39:32,111
I thought, "They're clearly having a mental breakdown."

896
00:39:33,081 --> 00:39:34,741
How many orders should we accept?

897
00:39:34,741 --> 00:39:36,651
What? Until the round ends.

898
00:39:37,211 --> 00:39:38,681
(1 order)

899
00:39:38,681 --> 00:39:40,481
For us, we kept getting orders.

900
00:39:41,451 --> 00:39:43,321
It felt like they had stopped.

901
00:39:46,721 --> 00:39:48,361
Eighteen-dollar price range.

902
00:39:49,021 --> 00:39:51,291
Currently, Number One...

903
00:39:52,431 --> 00:39:53,501
is ahead of...

904
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:56,331
Koony.

905
00:39:56,331 --> 00:39:59,971
(Current sales count: Number One, 50, Koony, 35)

906
00:40:01,041 --> 00:40:02,541
Okay, let's do this.

907
00:40:03,071 --> 00:40:04,411
You can do it.

908
00:40:04,741 --> 00:40:06,211
- We didn't have enough food...
- You can do it.

909
00:40:06,211 --> 00:40:07,241
to serve right away.

910
00:40:07,811 --> 00:40:10,381
(Checking the remaining meat)

911
00:40:10,581 --> 00:40:12,251
Even if we need to stop taking in orders for a bit,

912
00:40:12,421 --> 00:40:15,221
I should secure as much food as possible.

913
00:40:15,221 --> 00:40:16,251
That was what I thought.

914
00:40:16,921 --> 00:40:19,721
(Menu replenishment status: Guacamole)

915
00:40:19,721 --> 00:40:22,591
(Menu replenishment status: Hawaiian garlic shrimp noodles)

916
00:40:22,991 --> 00:40:24,331
Tae Hee, give them a lot of shrimps.

917
00:40:25,661 --> 00:40:27,431
- Tae Hee, potatoes are ready.
- Okay.

918
00:40:27,431 --> 00:40:29,001
(Menu replenishment status: Potato wedges)

919
00:40:29,201 --> 00:40:31,431
Sung Hoon, is pulled pork ready?

920
00:40:31,431 --> 00:40:33,141
Meat? I'll give it to you.

921
00:40:34,371 --> 00:40:36,471
- Give them a lot.
- Call their numbers.

922
00:40:36,471 --> 00:40:37,671
Yes. Give them a lot.

923
00:40:37,671 --> 00:40:39,881
(The lacking dishes have been replenished.)

924
00:40:40,311 --> 00:40:41,781
Undo the sold-out status.

925
00:40:41,781 --> 00:40:43,811
(Lee Sung Hoon resumes the business.)

926
00:40:44,151 --> 00:40:45,921
Okay, "Street Food Box."

927
00:40:45,921 --> 00:40:47,581
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

928
00:40:47,581 --> 00:40:48,781
Please confirm your order.

929
00:40:48,781 --> 00:40:50,491
- Are you giving it right away?
- Yes, you can take it now.

930
00:40:50,491 --> 00:40:52,821
- Take a fishcake and soup each.
- Thank you.

931
00:40:53,661 --> 00:40:55,561
You can order now.

932
00:40:56,591 --> 00:40:57,661
Give them a lot.

933
00:40:57,661 --> 00:40:58,761
Thank you for waiting so long.

934
00:40:58,761 --> 00:41:00,601
It's the perfect time to eat.

935
00:41:00,601 --> 00:41:02,331
Right, it's about time you crave supper.

936
00:41:02,331 --> 00:41:03,601
Let me close it for you.

937
00:41:03,701 --> 00:41:05,801
- Thank you. Enjoy.
- Thank you. I'll enjoy the food.

938
00:41:05,801 --> 00:41:07,701
Thank you. Enjoy.

939
00:41:08,241 --> 00:41:11,941
All orders will be closed after 15 minutes.

940
00:41:13,081 --> 00:41:16,481
(Meanwhile, Kwak Dong Hoon has been processing orders nonstop.)

941
00:41:16,851 --> 00:41:18,111
Why isn't it decreasing?

942
00:41:18,781 --> 00:41:20,221
- What isn't?
- The number of orders.

943
00:41:23,991 --> 00:41:25,651
You just need to do 35 more. The ongoing ones.

944
00:41:26,091 --> 00:41:28,091
I've done 33 so far.

945
00:41:28,921 --> 00:41:29,991
You can do it.

946
00:41:30,161 --> 00:41:32,161
The second half was a nightmare.

947
00:41:32,431 --> 00:41:34,531
The number of plates I've made throughout the nightmare...

948
00:41:34,931 --> 00:41:37,731
and the number of orders left to process were the same.

949
00:41:38,701 --> 00:41:40,071
It should end as you work on it.

950
00:41:40,071 --> 00:41:42,201
(Current sales status: 68)

951
00:41:42,201 --> 00:41:43,311
(Orders which need to be processed: 35)

952
00:41:43,311 --> 00:41:44,571
There's no end to this.

953
00:41:45,611 --> 00:41:49,381
(What's the result of the order rush?)

954
00:41:50,251 --> 00:41:52,011
Let's do our best for the second half as well.

955
00:41:52,011 --> 00:41:53,481
- Let's do this.
- Let's go.

956
00:41:53,951 --> 00:41:55,181
Let's go.

957
00:41:55,181 --> 00:41:57,621
(The 2nd half of 10-dollar price range starts.)

958
00:42:00,821 --> 00:42:01,991
People have already lined up in front of our stall.

959
00:42:03,291 --> 00:42:04,291
Oh, no.

960
00:42:05,529 --> 00:42:06,859
People have already lined up in front of our stall.

961
00:42:08,059 --> 00:42:09,059
Oh, no.

962
00:42:13,399 --> 00:42:14,499
Nice.

963
00:42:15,069 --> 00:42:16,339
I'm going to be generous with the cutlassfish bones, Mom.

964
00:42:16,639 --> 00:42:17,969
Let's give them more than enough.

965
00:42:19,309 --> 00:42:21,609
Since cutlassfish bones are a by-product, they're cheap.

966
00:42:21,809 --> 00:42:23,679
They can be used to increase the quantity.

967
00:42:24,009 --> 00:42:25,309
We'd be able to make them in bulk.

968
00:42:25,309 --> 00:42:27,949
They're the perfect simple snack to have with beer for dinner.

969
00:42:29,589 --> 00:42:31,749
(Spring mugwort wasabi mayo sauce)

970
00:42:31,989 --> 00:42:33,689
Cutlassfish on top.

971
00:42:33,689 --> 00:42:35,689
We're placing boneless cutlassfish sticks on top.

972
00:42:37,789 --> 00:42:40,459
(Deep-fried Jeju silver cutlassfish)

973
00:42:40,459 --> 00:42:41,529
(Gotgan)

974
00:42:41,529 --> 00:42:43,569
(Jeju silver cutlassfish fritters and crispy fish bones)

975
00:42:43,929 --> 00:42:45,299
The cutlassfish fritters sound good.

976
00:42:45,299 --> 00:42:46,399
Cutlassfish is already flavorful,

977
00:42:46,399 --> 00:42:47,739
so deep-frying it would intensify the taste.

978
00:42:48,699 --> 00:42:50,469
- This looks good.
- It's cutlassfish.

979
00:42:52,069 --> 00:42:54,879
(The menu customers were excited about even before opening)

980
00:42:55,739 --> 00:42:59,879
(Thanks to it, there's a long line at Gotgan.)

981
00:42:59,879 --> 00:43:00,879
(Gotgan)

982
00:43:02,619 --> 00:43:03,749
We have an order.

983
00:43:04,189 --> 00:43:05,449
(10 dollars)

984
00:43:07,389 --> 00:43:09,459
(The orders come in one after the other.)

985
00:43:09,929 --> 00:43:11,289
Okay, the orders are here.

986
00:43:11,689 --> 00:43:13,459
(Plating the cutlassfish bone fritters first)

987
00:43:13,459 --> 00:43:16,799
Here, Mom. Let's place five pieces of cutlassfish on top of each.

988
00:43:17,369 --> 00:43:18,599
- Five each?
- Yes, five each.

989
00:43:18,599 --> 00:43:20,769
(Warm boneless cutlassfish fritters after being deep-fried again)

990
00:43:21,169 --> 00:43:22,709
Number 1060, please!

991
00:43:23,509 --> 00:43:25,969
(Gotgan has started serving customers.)

992
00:43:25,969 --> 00:43:27,079
The batter.

993
00:43:28,139 --> 00:43:29,679
The line outside is no joke.

994
00:43:29,679 --> 00:43:31,279
I bet we'll sell like crazy.

995
00:43:31,809 --> 00:43:32,849
Let's go.

996
00:43:33,549 --> 00:43:36,549
(The line at the next-door booth is just as long.)

997
00:43:36,789 --> 00:43:38,089
Enjoy.

998
00:43:38,619 --> 00:43:39,889
Hi.

999
00:43:39,889 --> 00:43:41,559
It's cold, isn't it? Gosh.

1000
00:43:41,819 --> 00:43:43,589
- This is my first order.
- Is that so?

1001
00:43:43,589 --> 00:43:45,129
Please enjoy this warm stew.

1002
00:43:45,959 --> 00:43:47,399
It's the perfect menu for this weather.

1003
00:43:47,399 --> 00:43:48,929
- Right?
- Yes.

1004
00:43:49,329 --> 00:43:51,969
Since the weather has gotten cold, it's time for the soup.

1005
00:43:52,229 --> 00:43:53,299
It's cold.

1006
00:43:53,839 --> 00:43:56,539
Shouldn't there be warm food in the second half?

1007
00:43:56,969 --> 00:43:58,209
Like soup.

1008
00:43:58,939 --> 00:44:00,209
They're selling jjamppong soft tofu stew.

1009
00:44:01,379 --> 00:44:02,479
It's perfect for warming up.

1010
00:44:02,479 --> 00:44:04,509
There are so many lines somewhere else.

1011
00:44:04,979 --> 00:44:08,319
I'm sure you were craving soup now that it's gotten cold.

1012
00:44:08,819 --> 00:44:10,319
(The Star In My Heart)

1013
00:44:10,319 --> 00:44:12,089
(Half perilla and half jjamppong soft tofu stew)

1014
00:44:12,319 --> 00:44:15,859
For the soft tofu, we got fresh soy milk from a tofu place,

1015
00:44:16,019 --> 00:44:18,629
turned the heat off once the soy milk came to a boil,

1016
00:44:18,629 --> 00:44:21,459
and stirred it for 15 minutes after pouring in some coagulant.

1017
00:44:23,529 --> 00:44:26,839
(House-made soft tofu made from fresh soy milk)

1018
00:44:27,269 --> 00:44:29,709
(Perilla soft tofu)

1019
00:44:29,709 --> 00:44:34,479
(Jjamppong soft tofu)

1020
00:44:34,779 --> 00:44:36,649
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

1021
00:44:36,649 --> 00:44:38,209
(Served half and half)

1022
00:44:38,209 --> 00:44:39,849
Please wait a little. It won't take long.

1023
00:44:39,849 --> 00:44:40,879
- Oh, my.
- Hi.

1024
00:44:40,879 --> 00:44:42,349
You brought the crown.

1025
00:44:42,349 --> 00:44:43,689
Welcome.

1026
00:44:44,749 --> 00:44:47,719
We took a strategic approach.

1027
00:44:48,459 --> 00:44:50,359
As it's a beer festival,

1028
00:44:50,359 --> 00:44:53,059
we felt the need to prepare props, such as balloons and crowns,

1029
00:44:53,059 --> 00:44:55,959
for customers to decorate themselves.

1030
00:44:55,959 --> 00:44:57,899
"What? Where did they get that?"

1031
00:44:57,899 --> 00:45:00,739
Our strategy was to make the customers wonder.

1032
00:45:01,069 --> 00:45:02,139
(During the first half)

1033
